        { code: '    void Start()', what: '' },
        { code: '    {', what: '' },
        { code: '        body = GetComponent<Rigidbody2D>();', what: 'Finds the Rigidbody2D you added in the editor half and keeps the reference. `GetComponent<T>()` is the lookup from 2.1, and calling it once in `Start()` instead of every frame is the rule from 2.2.' , why: '**Without this line the movement in step 3 has nothing to write to.** The field would still be empty, and the Console fills with a NullReferenceException on the first frame, pointing at the line that uses the body. An empty reference is a valid value in C# — nothing complains until you use it.' },
        { code: '        target = waypointB;', what: 'Seeds the memory, so the enemy knows which way it is walking before the first frame runs. Either end works; starting toward B gives a full first beat.' , why: '**Leave this out and the first frame throws.** A field with no value is `null`, and the arrival check in step 3 asks that reference for its position. The memory needs a value before anything reads it, and the value has to come from somewhere that runs *once*.' },
        { code: '    }', what: '' },
      ],
    },
